{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>You</b> — the reason he mentioned the thing and its opposite: cleaving and drying up, and all upon the earth, and he mentioned that the seven boundaries stand forever and the inhabited world is not exchanged." "And the meaning of <b>summer and winter</b> — because most of the inhabited world is in the north side and some of it in the south side, and the reason to mention this with the boundaries of the earth is that when it is summer in one place, in another place it is winter."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 74, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:34:31.750998710Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}